  "id": "literal-replication",
  "term": "literal replication",
  "definition": "Literal replication is a type of dream incorporation in which something from waking life appears again in a dream in a direct, closely matching form. It contrasts with partial or indirect incorporations, where only some features of the waking event reappear.",
